1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
AccessProof: check common HTML accessibility gaps offline.
A source preflight, with human review still required.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The sample shows four potential barriers and two review prompts.
These counts describe source checks, not WCAG compliance.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Each finding includes element evidence and a repair pattern.
A placeholder-only field is a review prompt, not an unnamed-field error.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Write the review decision and mark the evidence reviewed.
The app keeps your local notes with unchanged evidence.

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Add an unnamed iframe and rescan: one new finding appears.
Before-and-after comparison separates new and retained evidence.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Source checks do not cover computed contrast or live interaction.
Use a rendered-page engine and test keyboard and screen-reader behavior.

7
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:43,000
English and Chinese views share the same local review.
Markdown and JSON exports preserve source and review notes.
